# Sections and cinematic effects

Full routines: `.agents/skills/new-section/SKILL.md` for a section, `.agents/skills/cinematic-3d-scroll/SKILL.md` for scroll, video and 3D. Read the one that fits before editing. The points below are the ones most often skipped.

## Any section
- Read the Design section of `AGENTS.md` first. Palette colours and the two typefaces only.
- Real copy. Ask for facts (prices, claims, quotes); never invent customers, reviews or statistics.
- One component per file under `components/`.
- One lead button per section, with a real destination. List any unwired button in the report.
- Check at 390px, 768px and 1440px in a browser: no horizontal scroll, tap targets of about 44px, nothing against the screen edge, card prices and buttons on one line.
- Layout options go on preview routes, and those routes are deleted once one is chosen.
- Report in three lines: what was built, the file, what needs the user's eyes.

## Scroll, video and 3D
- Budget: a background video hero plus at most two other techniques. Say what each adds and costs before coding.
- Under `prefers-reduced-motion`: no pinning, no scrubbing, no 3D download, no smooth scrolling.
- Below 768px, or if WebGL fails, show a still image in place of 3D.
- Load effect code only as its section nears the viewport.
- Ask before installing GSAP, Three.js or Lenis, and check current documentation for compatible versions.
- Afterwards, report the transfer size before and after.
